.TH ATHENAEUM-USERS 1 "June 2026" "Athenaeum" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
athenaeum-users \- manage local Athenaeum user accounts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B athenaeum users
.I command
.RI [ flags "] [" args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B users
subcommand of
.BR athenaeum (1)
manages local user accounts directly in the database, without starting the
server. It opens the SQLite database under the data directory and operates on
it offline, which is useful for bootstrapping, password recovery and
scripting.
.PP
User arguments may be given as a numeric id or as a username
(case-insensitive).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list\fR, \fBls
List all users with id, username, admin/guest/local flags, permissions and
creation time.
.TP
.BI "add, create " username " " \fR[ flags ]
Create a local user. Username must be at least 2 characters.
.TP
.BI "reset-password " user " " \fR[ flags ]
Reset a user's password. Aliases:
.BR passwd ", " password .
.TP
.BI "rename " "user new-username"
Rename a user.
.TP
.BI "set-admin " user " " \fR[ flags ]
Grant or revoke admin privileges. Alias:
.BR admin .
.TP
.BI "set-permissions " user " " \fB\-\-set " list"
Set non-admin permissions. Alias:
.BR permissions .
.TP
.BI "show, get " user
Show details for one user.
.TP
.BI "delete, rm " user " " \fR[ flags ]
Delete a user.
.TP
.B help
Show built-in help.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-data " dir"
Data directory containing
.IR athenaeum.db .
Applies to every command.
Environment:
.BR ATHENAEUM_DATA .
Default:
.BR ./data .
.TP
.BI \-\-color " mode"
CLI color mode:
.BR auto ", " always ", or " never .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color.
.TP
.BI \-\-password " value"
Password for
.B add
and
.BR reset-password .
See PASSWORD SOURCES.
.TP
.B \-\-admin
For
.BR add ", grant admin on creation. For " set-admin ", grant admin."
.TP
.B \-\-no\-admin
For
.BR set-admin ", revoke admin."
.TP
.BI \-\-set " list"
For
.BR set-permissions ", a comma-separated permission list. Valid values:"
.BR read ", " edit_metadata ", " delete_books ", " manage_library ", " manage_users .
.TP
.B \-\-revoke\-sessions
For
.BR reset-password ", revoke active sessions after the reset. Default: true."
.TP
.B \-\-force
For
.BR delete ", skip the interactive confirmation prompt."
.SH PASSWORD SOURCES
For
.B add
and
.BR reset-password ,
the password is resolved in this order:
.IP 1. 4
The
.B \-\-password
flag value.
.IP 2. 4
The
.B ATHENAEUM_PASSWORD
environment variable.
.IP 3. 4
A single line read from standard input when neither of the above is set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List users from a specific data directory:
.B athenaeum users list \-\-data ./data
.TP
Create a user with an explicit password:
.B athenaeum users add alice \-\-password 'secretpass'
.TP
Reset an admin password:
.B athenaeum users reset-password admin \-\-password 'newpass'
.TP
Revoke admin from a user:
.B athenaeum users set-admin bob \-\-no\-admin
.TP
Grant limited permissions to a non-admin:
.B athenaeum users set-permissions carol \-\-set read,edit_metadata
.TP
Delete a user by id without confirmation:
.B athenaeum users delete 3 \-\-force
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR athenaeum (1)
